  "proof": [
    "The genuine radial factor has the actual positive germ ((3/2)*chi)^(2/3)=Q*chi^(2/3), with Q=(3/2)^(2/3) fixed before all states/components. The pinned constant-scalar ordinary-jet identity transfers the existing chi power estimates.",
    "At the axis (0,theta), every jet of the first projection has norm at most one, including order zero because that value is zero. The true pointwise Leibniz inequality therefore bounds the radial coordinate jets by 2^n*Q times the same finite power-jet prefix. No neighborhood radius is used as a numerical estimate.",
    "Only positive-order jets of the whole chart are requested. The angular coordinate is the actual even displacement plus snd; the latter has positive jets at most one. Its unbounded angular zero-order value is not assumed bounded.",
    "The complete max-norm chart bound is (2+Q*2^n)*M. A_n=1+sum_{k<=n}(BE_k+BP_k) dominates both input families and combines their actual material scales by max. The common loss is max(lossEven,lossPower) and the common low order also includes the actual chi positivity input.",
    "The final B_n=1+A_n+(2+Q*2^n)*A_n controls coefficient and exponent before state, component, actual host, factor representative, localization radius, parameter scale, flow and angle. The high grading stays linear and its order is n+one common loss.",
    "All regularity is for the same actual unscaled flow and original n01RootLabel, yielding the genuine extended even/odd fields. No new extension, model, arbitrary compact interval or inverse R/delta cost is substituted."
  ],
  "scope_caveat": "Raw component optical lower, actual host containment and OrdinaryFlowJacobianBounds remain explicit upstream hypotheses, not consequences asserted for arbitrary Through03. This output is the actual unit-model positive ordinary spatial chart tower; stored old-K physical identification, all parameter SmoothDirections and final N04c estimates remain separate.",
  "self_review": "Read all source and actual contracts. Checked zero-order fst separately, actual positive power germ, fixed-pinned Nat.sum_range_choose and max-norm product API, finite-prefix/scale/low/loss quantifier order. No compiler/elaborator/CI invoked.",
